Subject: Persist Krypton workspace tab membership through Chromium sessions

KryptonUI provides named workspaces within a Chromium profile. Keep membership
on the original WebContents and carry it through session command rebuilding,
full restore, and Recently Closed tab/window records. Restore metadata before
inserting tabs so the native shell never assigns a restored tab to whichever
workspace happens to be active during startup. The selected restored tab names
the active workspace; no closed-window-only metadata is needed.

Helium has no equivalent workspace feature. These hooks are enabled only for
KryptonUI and preserve Chromium's browser/profile and tab ownership. The owned
workspace catalog, models and metadata helpers live in chromium_src.

